WEBVTT

01:31.591 --> 01:32.674
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS

01:32.675 --> 01:33.884
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS

01:33.885 --> 01:36.220
Hey, have you heard the rumors?

01:36.221 --> 01:39.515
<i>About that evil woman
who stirred up a rebellion?</i>

01:39.516 --> 01:42.226
<i>The imperial younger brother
commanded the Forbidden Army</i>

01:42.227 --> 01:43.561
<i>to punish the wicked ones, eh?</i>

01:44.145 --> 01:46.104
<i>But that villainess named Loulan</i>

01:46.105 --> 01:48.983
<i>apparently scarred
the imperial younger brother's face.</i>

01:50.110 --> 01:51.486
<i>That's harsh.</i>

01:54.572 --> 01:55.532
Sir Jinshi.

01:56.407 --> 01:57.325
What?

01:57.909 --> 02:00.869
These are circulating through town.

02:00.870 --> 02:04.206
They're writing about you
and the revolt of the Shi clan

02:04.207 --> 02:05.875
in a rather unrestrained manner.

02:07.836 --> 02:09.294
Leave it alone.

02:09.295 --> 02:10.337
Yes, sir.

02:10.338 --> 02:12.090
And this one's from that girl.

02:13.341 --> 02:14.425
From Maomao?

02:18.847 --> 02:22.809
<i>My apothecary closes
when the Verdigris House opens.</i>

02:23.518 --> 02:25.894
<i>Good customers don't come at night.</i>

02:25.895 --> 02:28.314
<i>Lighting the lamps is a waste of oil.</i>

02:32.610 --> 02:33.735
Grams.

02:33.736 --> 02:34.653
What?

02:34.654 --> 02:37.156
Today's sales. Do your thing.

02:37.157 --> 02:38.448
Got it.

02:38.449 --> 02:40.702
Chou-u, time to go.

02:41.369 --> 02:43.329
What, already?

02:47.292 --> 02:48.585
It's freezing…

02:50.086 --> 02:52.004
What, aren't you going to eat?

02:52.005 --> 02:53.715
I'm eating…

02:56.217 --> 02:57.635
Get out of bed.

02:58.553 --> 02:59.887
Meanie!

02:59.888 --> 03:01.890
Shut up and put this on.

03:05.351 --> 03:07.352
I want more meat.

03:07.353 --> 03:09.272
Then start making money.

03:09.939 --> 03:13.150
<i>I'm getting enough funds
to support Chou-u,</i>

03:13.151 --> 03:14.986
<i>but I don't intend to waste it.</i>

03:15.570 --> 03:18.947
Come on, Freckles. You make tons of money.

03:18.948 --> 03:20.866
Why don't we eat something better?

03:20.867 --> 03:24.745
Listen, dummy.
I borrow space for my shop from Grams.

03:24.746 --> 03:26.831
Rent is more expensive than you think.

03:29.459 --> 03:30.709
I'm cold…

03:30.710 --> 03:33.254
<i>That winter garment
sure does look pretty cold.</i>

03:34.589 --> 03:36.924
I'm shopping for clothes tomorrow.
Come along.

03:36.925 --> 03:38.175
Huh? Really?

03:38.176 --> 03:39.260
All right!

03:40.637 --> 03:42.138
That hurt!

03:47.101 --> 03:48.603
Don't wander off.

03:51.731 --> 03:54.733
<i>This main street
divides the capital into East and West.</i>

03:54.734 --> 03:57.861
<i>As you advance north, the shops get nicer.</i>

03:57.862 --> 04:00.657
<i>The further south, the lower the quality.</i>

04:02.033 --> 04:05.370
<i>The byroads are also packed
with suspicious street vendors.</i>

04:06.204 --> 04:07.914
I said don't wander off.

04:12.043 --> 04:13.335
Here we are.

04:13.336 --> 04:15.712
Come on, secondhand clothes?

04:15.713 --> 04:17.422
Don't be greedy.

04:17.423 --> 04:19.676
Okay, winter garments for kids…

04:21.552 --> 04:22.887
What's that one?

04:27.267 --> 04:29.560
<i>Looks like a barbarian tribe's garment.</i>

04:30.061 --> 04:32.063
Looks kind of shabby, huh?

04:32.855 --> 04:33.856
Ouch!

04:36.234 --> 04:38.068
Looks shabby, does it?

04:38.069 --> 04:39.736
Isn't it, though?

04:39.737 --> 04:43.490
Young girls' clothes
should have more vibrant colors, right?

04:43.491 --> 04:45.785
Normally, yeah, I suppose.

04:46.327 --> 04:49.663
You see, this is a robe
worn by a heavenly maiden.

04:49.664 --> 04:51.082
Heavenly maiden?

04:51.666 --> 04:55.168
A gorgeous heavenly maiden
who disappeared in a lake.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.296
Wanna hear the legend?

04:57.588 --> 04:58.505
I sure do!

04:58.506 --> 05:01.467
<i>The owner here is a chatterbox.</i>

05:02.051 --> 05:04.721
<i>Pretty sure my old man
fell into his trap too.</i>

05:08.016 --> 05:11.811
This story takes place
in a certain western village.

05:13.313 --> 05:16.983
<i>One day, a villager rescued
a young girl who lost her way.</i>

05:17.984 --> 05:22.947
<i>She was incredibly beautiful
with golden hair and fair skin.</i>

05:23.573 --> 05:26.326
<i>For the villager,
it was love at first sight.</i>

05:28.077 --> 05:32.707
<i>To thank him for saving her,
the girl wove a robe for the villager.</i>

05:34.167 --> 05:37.335
<i>That robe,
embroidered with a strange design,</i>

05:37.336 --> 05:41.423
<i>apparently sold for several times
the price of other fabrics.</i>

05:41.424 --> 05:46.928
<i>As months passed, the girl cried
and desperately yearned to return home,</i>

05:46.929 --> 05:49.931
<i>but the smitten villager
repeatedly proposed</i>

05:49.932 --> 05:53.061
<i>until she finally agreed to marry him.</i>

05:54.562 --> 05:55.896
<i>Shortly after,</i>

05:55.897 --> 05:58.900
<i>the girl's family
came to the village searching for her.</i>

05:59.609 --> 06:02.111
<i>The villager didn't want to let her go.</i>

06:02.612 --> 06:04.112
<i>He concealed her,</i>

06:04.113 --> 06:07.533
<i>and all of the villagers
feigned ignorance.</i>

06:08.326 --> 06:11.328
<i>The girl's family
withdrew for the time being</i>

06:11.329 --> 06:13.081
<i>but seemed to harbor suspicion.</i>

06:13.998 --> 06:18.419
<i>And so, the villager decided
to carry out the wedding ceremony at once.</i>

06:19.128 --> 06:23.216
<i>The girl sensed her family and refused,
but the villager showed no mercy.</i>

06:23.883 --> 06:26.176
<i>He made her cleanse in the village spring</i>

06:26.177 --> 06:30.973
<i>and wear a wedding gown
she'd woven in the style of her homeland.</i>

06:31.891 --> 06:34.601
<i>Her tears showed no signs of drying up.</i>

06:34.602 --> 06:36.687
<i>Her entire body was soaked in them.</i>

06:38.898 --> 06:44.402
<i>One last time, the girl begged
to be returned to her family.</i>

06:44.403 --> 06:46.072
<i>But when he refused…</i>

06:57.625 --> 07:00.502
<i>All that remained
was a single piece of cloth,</i>

07:00.503 --> 07:03.964
<i>the veil that she'd worn on her head.</i>

07:03.965 --> 07:06.424
<i>She returned to the heavens.</i>

07:06.425 --> 07:09.178
<i>That's what the villagers
apparently believed.</i>

07:10.012 --> 07:14.934
And this is the very robe
woven by the heavenly maiden herself.

07:16.936 --> 07:21.190
Hey, Freckles. This is awesome!
Why don't you buy it?

07:22.275 --> 07:26.069
Miss, since you're probably
the same age as the heavenly maiden,

07:26.070 --> 07:27.237
here's a discount.

07:27.238 --> 07:28.655
Pricey!

07:28.656 --> 07:30.323
<i>Off by a whole digit…</i>

07:30.324 --> 07:33.785
What, you don't believe
the legend of the heavenly maiden?

07:33.786 --> 07:35.370
Where's your sense of wonder?

07:35.371 --> 07:37.331
<i>Says the guy who's trying to scam us.</i>

07:37.999 --> 07:41.252
<i>I've already seen
a heavenly maiden vanish in the water.</i>

07:44.338 --> 07:46.256
Can I touch that?

07:46.257 --> 07:49.010
Fine, but don't get any filth on it.

07:49.719 --> 07:53.513
<i>Various oddities exist in this world,</i>

07:53.514 --> 07:56.224
<i>but they always have a place of origin.</i>

07:56.225 --> 07:58.602
<i>Since nobody knows the origin,</i>

07:58.603 --> 08:00.562
<i>people try convincing themselves</i>

08:00.563 --> 08:03.483
<i>by blaming curses, wizardry,
or sometimes even ghosts.</i>

08:05.109 --> 08:06.777
This design…

08:07.862 --> 08:11.239
Hey, what would you do
if I sold this for ten times this price?

08:11.240 --> 08:12.533
Ten times?

08:13.284 --> 08:16.787
If you could do that,
I'd give you all my clothes for free.

08:18.539 --> 08:20.040
Hear that, Chou-u?

08:20.041 --> 08:21.917
Ten times?

08:21.918 --> 08:24.002
Nobody's gonna pay that much.

08:24.003 --> 08:26.088
What's with the crazy talk, Freckles?

08:27.006 --> 08:29.925
Owner, let me borrow
this robe and some charcoal.

08:29.926 --> 08:31.677
Hey! What are you doing?

08:39.894 --> 08:42.939
Stop! Are you trying to char
my precious goods?

08:45.024 --> 08:47.026
It's not charred…

08:47.985 --> 08:49.861
That's charcoal, right?

08:49.862 --> 08:51.029
But how?

08:51.030 --> 08:53.449
Miss, what on earth…

08:54.033 --> 08:56.368
You said it yourself, didn't you?

08:56.369 --> 08:59.955
This robe was woven by a heavenly maiden!

08:59.956 --> 09:01.373
Heavenly maiden?

09:01.374 --> 09:03.250
Now, as you can see,

09:03.251 --> 09:06.461
charcoal can't burn this
or even leave a scorch mark.

09:06.462 --> 09:08.881
This bizarre miracle robe is…

09:10.258 --> 09:11.092
What?

09:13.553 --> 09:14.678
That's right!

09:14.679 --> 09:19.809
It's the legendary "fire rat cloak"
woven by a heavenly maiden!

09:20.476 --> 09:22.185
Let me take a look!

09:22.186 --> 09:23.186
How much?

09:23.187 --> 09:24.729
Ten! I'll give you ten!

09:24.730 --> 09:26.273
No, 20.

09:26.274 --> 09:27.525
I'll pay 50!

09:28.568 --> 09:31.069
Freckles, I'm so hot…

09:31.070 --> 09:32.445
Take them off, then.

09:32.446 --> 09:35.782
You're the one who opted
to wear them instead of carrying them.

09:35.783 --> 09:39.494
<i>I would've preferred softer colors,</i>

09:39.495 --> 09:42.706
<i>but I got them for free,
so I can't complain.</i>

09:42.707 --> 09:45.376
So, why didn't that robe burn?

09:46.127 --> 09:48.628
Do you know what clothes are made from?

09:48.629 --> 09:50.922
Cotton, hemp fibers, and stuff?

09:50.923 --> 09:52.382
Bugs too.

09:52.383 --> 09:55.594
Yeah, but that robe was made of stone.

09:55.595 --> 09:57.178
Stone?

09:57.179 --> 09:58.973
Stones like these?

09:59.557 --> 10:01.976
Stones come in various shapes too.

10:02.476 --> 10:05.438
Clothing made from fibrous stone
won't burn easily.

10:06.272 --> 10:09.816
<i>Nonflammable cloth woven from asbestos
is called "huohuanbu,"</i>

10:09.817 --> 10:12.570
<i>also known as "fire rat cloak."</i>

10:13.738 --> 10:18.200
<i>They might have heard of its existence,
but most people have never seen it.</i>

10:19.285 --> 10:22.537
Okay… Then what about
the story of the heavenly maiden?

10:22.538 --> 10:26.416
I guess that's a half-truth
and a half-lie.

10:26.417 --> 10:27.460
What the heck?

10:28.669 --> 10:31.797
<i>I recognized the embroidery
on the robe's cuff.</i>

10:32.465 --> 10:35.759
<i>They're foreign characters
that my old man often drew.</i>

10:35.760 --> 10:38.596
<i>When written stylistically,
the design looks like a vine.</i>

10:39.388 --> 10:43.601
<i>The so-called heavenly maiden
probably came from a foreign land.</i>

10:44.310 --> 10:48.313
<i>I dunno whether she was really lost
or if somebody kidnapped her,</i>

10:48.314 --> 10:51.567
<i>but she wove that robe
with a deep desire to go home.</i>

10:52.360 --> 10:56.237
<i>By embroidering a design
with characters illegible to the villager,</i>

10:56.238 --> 10:58.908
<i>she secretly appealed
to her compatriots for help.</i>

11:00.660 --> 11:04.579
Right, so that's why
her family came to get her.

11:04.580 --> 11:06.040
Then, on her wedding day,

11:06.791 --> 11:10.460
<i>while "cleansing" in the spring,
she soaked her undergarment</i>

11:10.461 --> 11:13.089
<i>and donned the asbestos robe on top of it.</i>

11:14.256 --> 11:15.340
<i>Did you know?</i>

11:15.341 --> 11:19.302
<i>A wooden bowl filled with water won't burn
until the water fully evaporates.</i>

11:19.303 --> 11:21.096
<i>It's the same idea.</i>

11:21.097 --> 11:25.892
<i>Furthermore, if you layer
flammable garments over the white robe,</i>

11:25.893 --> 11:28.521
<i>even big flames
won't reach the body right away.</i>

11:29.480 --> 11:33.025
<i>All she had to do was jump in the spring
before she got burned.</i>

11:33.609 --> 11:36.194
Why didn't you tell the dude at the shop?

11:36.195 --> 11:38.447
He values a sense of wonder, right?

11:39.448 --> 11:40.908
I don't get it…

11:43.119 --> 11:44.953
<i>A foreign girl.</i>

11:44.954 --> 11:48.332
<i>Would it even be possible
for a completely ordinary girl</i>

11:48.916 --> 11:52.169
<i>to send messages through embroidery
and set herself on fire?</i>

11:53.087 --> 11:56.340
<i>She could read and write.
She had knowledge of asbestos too.</i>

11:57.049 --> 12:00.886
<i>Why would a girl like that
be wandering around in a foreign land?</i>

12:02.596 --> 12:05.433
<i>Western countries often fight each other.</i>

12:06.350 --> 12:07.517
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

12:07.518 --> 12:11.689
<i>the two envoys visiting the country of Li
behaved suspiciously as well.</i>

12:12.773 --> 12:16.819
<i>One of them seemed to have
a connection with the Shi clan.</i>

12:18.070 --> 12:22.158
<i>The so-called heavenly maiden
could have been a spy or something.</i>

12:23.033 --> 12:24.243
<i>Or maybe not.</i>

12:25.369 --> 12:27.288
Hey, Freckles?

12:37.548 --> 12:39.175
Hello, and welcome!

12:40.176 --> 12:41.468
What?

12:41.469 --> 12:44.846
Xiaomao, have you mistaken
the man next to me for someone else?

12:44.847 --> 12:46.348
This is Sir Jinshi, you know.

12:51.228 --> 12:52.313
Come on in.

12:54.398 --> 12:57.442
<i>It's thinned out
since those stitches came out,</i>

12:57.443 --> 12:59.861
<i>but I guess it left a scar after all.</i>

12:59.862 --> 13:02.071
Didn't you have something to tell me?

13:02.072 --> 13:02.948
<i>Right.</i>

13:03.532 --> 13:04.909
Please look at this.

13:05.534 --> 13:06.576
What is it?

13:06.577 --> 13:08.411
Some opportunistic looter

13:08.412 --> 13:12.040
stole this from the Shi clan's stronghold
and sold it off.

13:12.041 --> 13:13.334
How did you find it?

13:13.834 --> 13:16.336
I found it by coincidence at a bookstore.

13:16.337 --> 13:20.382
<i>Ukyou did me a favor and collected
all the ones sold in other towns.</i>

13:21.592 --> 13:24.594
Ukyou, can I leave this man in your care?

13:24.595 --> 13:27.889
Sure, I could use
some extra help right now.

13:27.890 --> 13:30.309
But Chou-u knows him, right?

13:30.851 --> 13:32.520
Yeah, that's a problem.

13:33.020 --> 13:34.813
Then I'll change my name.

13:35.397 --> 13:37.191
I won't miss my old name.

13:37.733 --> 13:38.943
Let's see.

13:39.568 --> 13:40.778
How about "Sazen"?

13:41.529 --> 13:45.240
What's so special about this book
that "Sazen" guy sold?

13:45.241 --> 13:48.576
The other books of this series
are in the stronghold, I think.

13:48.577 --> 13:50.703
I want you to gather them for me.

13:50.704 --> 13:52.081
Why do you want them?

13:52.665 --> 13:53.791
Well…

13:55.417 --> 13:56.793
because of this.

13:56.794 --> 13:58.086
What are those?

13:58.087 --> 13:59.754
Simmered locusts.

13:59.755 --> 14:02.173
They're mostly grasshoppers, though.

14:02.174 --> 14:04.343
No… I'm not eating those!

14:04.927 --> 14:06.512
I didn't ask you to.

14:07.513 --> 14:10.391
There was an outbreak of grasshoppers
last year.

14:11.016 --> 14:14.270
Haven't the farmers told you
about a locust plague?

14:16.105 --> 14:18.189
I've received that report.

14:18.190 --> 14:20.234
There was extensive damage
to northern farmlands.

14:20.943 --> 14:24.238
<i>But not bad enough
to cause any death from starvation.</i>

14:24.947 --> 14:26.698
To make up for the poor harvests,

14:26.699 --> 14:30.201
we decided to draw on reserves
from Binan-shu in the south.

14:30.202 --> 14:31.911
In Binan-shu?

14:31.912 --> 14:32.746
Yes.

14:33.330 --> 14:38.127
<i>We sought help from the Bi clan,
to which they graciously agreed.</i>

14:38.836 --> 14:40.086
I see.

14:40.087 --> 14:44.132
However, locust damage
could continue for several years.

14:44.133 --> 14:47.595
If it happens again this year,
things are looking bleak.

14:48.178 --> 14:49.889
You're certainly right.

14:50.681 --> 14:52.265
<i>When locust plagues happen,</i>

14:52.266 --> 14:56.103
<i>people blame the Emperor
for not ruling the country properly.</i>

14:57.271 --> 14:59.397
<i>People are ridiculously superstitious.</i>

14:59.398 --> 15:02.275
<i>If this happens
a year after destroying the Shi clan,</i>

15:02.276 --> 15:04.278
<i>what would the people think?</i>

15:05.279 --> 15:10.117
<i>It might completely reverse
the contents of those books going around.</i>

15:11.076 --> 15:14.078
<i>Sir Jinshi probably realizes that too.</i>

15:14.079 --> 15:16.540
Locust plagues are an act of nature.

15:17.124 --> 15:19.125
What are we supposed to do?

15:19.126 --> 15:21.669
Build fires to lure the bugs in?

15:21.670 --> 15:24.380
Or squish them all one by one?

15:24.381 --> 15:27.051
That's why I'm looking for these.

15:27.718 --> 15:31.805
These illustrations were left
by that stronghold's previous apothecary.

15:32.389 --> 15:35.517
Apparently, the apothecary was researching
ways to prevent locust plagues.

15:36.352 --> 15:37.352
Seriously?

15:37.353 --> 15:38.436
INSECTS: PART I

15:38.437 --> 15:40.271
Locusts aren't listed in this one.

15:40.272 --> 15:43.274
There should be another volume
about insects.

15:43.275 --> 15:45.611
I think it's still in the stronghold.

15:47.529 --> 15:51.032
Although I don't know
how far the research advanced,

15:51.033 --> 15:52.534
it's worth looking into.

15:54.161 --> 15:55.078
Gaoshun.

15:55.079 --> 15:58.958
Yes, sir. I'll arrange for it
to be obtained in the next few days.

15:59.541 --> 16:02.670
<i>For now, I've told him
everything he needs to know.</i>

16:05.422 --> 16:06.757
Are you tired, sir?

16:08.634 --> 16:10.885
Well, I suppose so.

16:10.886 --> 16:12.179
But I'm fine.

16:14.807 --> 16:17.393
<i>At this rate, he's going to keel over.</i>

16:18.435 --> 16:19.353
What?

16:20.062 --> 16:21.689
<i>He should just sleep.</i>

16:22.314 --> 16:24.482
<i>If he's that exhausted,</i>

16:24.483 --> 16:28.153
<i>he should just get some rest
and let his errand boys do the work.</i>

16:29.029 --> 16:31.824
Would you like to rest, Sir Jinshi?

16:32.408 --> 16:34.033
What kind of question is that?

16:34.034 --> 16:36.035
I'll prepare a bed straightaway.

16:36.036 --> 16:37.286
Please go to sleep.

16:37.287 --> 16:38.122
Right here?

16:38.706 --> 16:40.207
Afraid to sleep alone?

16:42.292 --> 16:44.752
That was a joke. Please wait a moment--

16:44.753 --> 16:46.380
Yeah, I can't sleep alone.

16:49.967 --> 16:52.720
<i>I see. Looks like he gets lonely.</i>

16:54.972 --> 16:58.183
Understood, sir. Please wait a moment.

17:02.271 --> 17:04.397
That takes time to prepare.

17:04.398 --> 17:05.357
I know.

17:06.358 --> 17:08.568
It's a 30-minute wait.

17:08.569 --> 17:10.738
<i>That's enough time to prepare it?</i>

17:12.531 --> 17:13.823
Right this way.

17:13.824 --> 17:16.285
Please get some rest here, sir.

17:16.869 --> 17:19.872
Work is important,
but rest is also essential.

17:20.622 --> 17:21.956
If you fancy a warm bath,

17:21.957 --> 17:24.710
we've prepared a medicated bath next door.

17:25.294 --> 17:27.212
Please use this sleepwear.

17:27.796 --> 17:28.922
Okay.

17:29.506 --> 17:31.425
<i>The heavenly maiden smile is gone,</i>

17:32.009 --> 17:34.595
<i>but his otherworldly beauty holds up well.</i>

17:37.723 --> 17:39.725
I'll have a sleeping partner, correct?

17:40.225 --> 17:41.225
Yes.

17:41.226 --> 17:42.811
I'll go bathe now.

17:44.146 --> 17:44.980
Enjoy.

17:54.656 --> 17:57.200
Why are there
scantily clad girls in there?

17:57.201 --> 17:59.661
They're pro masseuses. Not your thing?

18:01.455 --> 18:03.706
It's just a massage, right?

18:03.707 --> 18:05.875
They usually do more than that.

18:05.876 --> 18:07.585
I'll pass on the bath.

18:07.586 --> 18:09.129
Should I help you dress?

18:09.755 --> 18:11.090
I'll do it myself.

18:17.638 --> 18:19.889
<i>He's still got that buff physique.</i>

18:19.890 --> 18:23.435
<i>Despite being busy,
I guess he still makes time to train.</i>

18:25.938 --> 18:27.147
Here you go.

18:28.148 --> 18:30.067
What's this? Sleep medication?

18:30.859 --> 18:32.194
A performance enhancer.

18:36.031 --> 18:38.491
What do I need a performance enhancer for?

18:38.492 --> 18:42.371
Because I heard
it's the best thing for fatigued men.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.833
Do you understand what that sounds like?

18:46.416 --> 18:48.293
What did you think I meant?

18:51.547 --> 18:56.135
<i>Even though he's a man,
maybe I should've worded that discreetly.</i>

18:56.718 --> 18:58.137
Now, Sir Jinshi…

19:00.722 --> 19:01.973
If I may ask…

19:01.974 --> 19:03.809
Go… on.

19:05.853 --> 19:08.397
What kind of girls are you into?

19:17.364 --> 19:18.824
What's this about?

19:19.408 --> 19:22.786
Ms. Suiren told me
you prefer girls around your age.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.789
Don't worry. They're all virgins.

19:27.416 --> 19:29.709
Are none of them your type?

19:29.710 --> 19:32.337
I'd rather just sleep right now.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.130
Let me sleep.

19:34.131 --> 19:35.339
Okay, which girl--

19:35.340 --> 19:36.550
I mean "sleep" literally!

19:39.219 --> 19:41.137
Would you like one instead?

19:41.138 --> 19:43.055
I'm a henpecked husband.

19:43.056 --> 19:44.849
And my daughter is a clean freak.

19:44.850 --> 19:46.267
<i>I see.</i>

19:46.268 --> 19:49.854
<i>I probably shouldn't have offered
courtesans to a married man.</i>

19:49.855 --> 19:53.149
She tells me,
"Papa, you're dirty. Take your bath last."

19:53.150 --> 19:55.026
Do you know what that feels like?

19:55.027 --> 19:56.695
I understand…

19:57.237 --> 19:58.697
<i>how the daughter feels.</i>

20:07.915 --> 20:10.334
Now then, please excuse me.

20:17.507 --> 20:19.593
At least sing me a lullaby.

20:31.980 --> 20:33.398
I'm a bad singer.

20:33.899 --> 20:35.067
I don't mind.

20:42.908 --> 20:45.661
<i>Kitty cat, kitty cat</i>

20:46.286 --> 20:49.206
<i>Kitty cat, kitty cat</i>

20:49.831 --> 20:56.213
<i>She cries and cries
Wondering where that child is</i>

20:57.130 --> 21:03.762
<i>The little birds that know nothing</i>

21:04.554 --> 21:08.557
<i>Flew higher and higher</i>

21:08.558 --> 21:11.228
<i>Up in the sky</i>

21:11.895 --> 21:14.648
<i>Kitty cat, kitty cat</i>

21:15.399 --> 21:18.277
<i>Kitty cat, kitty cat</i>

21:18.819 --> 21:22.989
<i>Sweet dreams for now</i>

21:22.990 --> 21:26.576
<i>See you tomorrow</i>

21:33.667 --> 21:35.668
<i>His face regained its color,</i>

21:35.669 --> 21:38.964
<i>and he inhaled three bowls
of rice porridge, so I'm sure he's fine.</i>

21:39.464 --> 21:40.507
Maomao.

21:42.259 --> 21:43.468
Big Sis Pairin.

21:43.969 --> 21:46.179
Why don't you just accept it already?

21:48.223 --> 21:49.891
No clue what you mean.

22:07.284 --> 22:08.452
Here you go.

23:46.007 --> 23:52.806
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

23:54.516 --> 23:57.185
<i>The next episode is "Let Them Eat Cake."</i>

23:58.019 --> 24:00.856
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
